I am having trouble getting command line parameters passed when running 
an executable.  The executable is a compiled C source code, which has the 
necessary argc,argv code to handle a command line argument, but whenever 
I try to run with my command line arguments:
  run foo.exe 3500
I get an error on the 3500 stating that too many parameters have been 
used, reenter command with less parameters.  Is there a compiler or 
linker flag which must be set to allow extra parameters?  I am working on 
a VAX 4100, running OpenVMS 6.1, and compiled using the standard DEC C 
libraries, which appear to have all the C lib functions I need.  What am 
I missing?

Thanks in advance...
-Carl J Lambrecht
 Kinesis Computing, Inc.






