:  run foo.exe 3500
:I get an error on the 3500 stating that too many parameters have been 
:used, reenter command with less parameters.  Is there a compiler or 
:linker flag which must be set to allow extra parameters?  I am working on 
:a VAX 4100, running OpenVMS 6.1, and compiled using the standard DEC C 
:libraries, which appear to have all the C lib functions I need.  What am 
:I missing?

  You're missing the discussion of foreign commands in the DEC C manual. 
  (Don't you hate it when that happens? :-)  Prior to OpenVMS V6.2 and
  the introduction of the DCL$PATH command path support, one had to set
  up a foreign command in order to use C's argument-passing (argc and
  argv) mechanism.   ("Passing Arguments to the main Function" is the
  heading in the _DEC C User's Guide for OpenVMS Systems_ manual.)

  A foreign command is a DCL (global) symbol that equates to a full device,
  directory and filename specification preceded by a "$" -- preceded by
  the "this is a foreign command" indicator character. 

  eg: "fc :== $sys$sysdevice:[000000]imagename.exe"

  The above C program can now retrieve the arguments via argc and argv.
  (The OpenVMS V6.2 DCL$PATH support is far more convenient.)

